precedence is already documented.\\n- 应答：The precedence is documented, but the current operator experience does not clearly expose which rule won for a specific inbound message.\\n\\n5. objection：This belongs in docs, not an issue.\\n- 应答：A docs improvement would help, but an issue is still useful to request a diagnostics/observability surface if maintainers agree that current inspection is insufficient.\\n\\n6. objection：You need stronger reproduction before claiming a product problem.\\n- 应答：Agreed, which is why the framing avoids “wrong routing” and focuses on explainability of the observed outcome.\\n\\n7. objection：The session key already shows which agent handled the message.\\n- 应答：Yes, but the canonical session key reflects the selected agent after routing; it does not explain which routing rule won.\\n\\n三、结论：P1 先发 issue，还是先发 docs PR\\n- 明确判断：**先发 P1 issue，再发 docs PR。**\\n\\n四、判断依据\\n1. P1 的核心价值在于把问题定义为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是写死在某一页文档上。\\n2. 如果先发 docs PR，maintainer 很可能只把它当“文案补充”，不会正面回应“是否需要暴露 winning routing rule”。\\n3. 先发 issue 更利于争取一个明确态度：\\n- maintainers 是否认同当前可解释性不足；\\n- 是否愿意增加日志/诊断输出；\\n- 还是仅希望通过 docs 解决。\\n4. docs PR 适合作为 P1 issue 的后续动作：当 maintainer 接受“这里确实难解释”后，再补 group routing 与 canonical session key 的澄清文档，更顺。\\n\\n原因：从 maintainer 视角，最容易打回的是“你把 expected behavior 误报成 bug”。所以要先把 issue 写成一个低冲突、可接受的 diagnostics gap 讨论入口。只要 issue 站稳，docs PR 就会更容易被接。\\n建议：\\n1. P1 issue 正文里主动放这句：\\n`This report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer operator-facing way to confirm which routing rule won.`\\n2. 标题坚持用：\\n`Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent`\\n3. P2 docs PR 暂时作为跟进项，不抢在 issue 前面发。\",\n                \"timeoutSeconds\": 20\n              },\n              \"partialJson\": \"{\\\"sessionKey\\\":\\\"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"状态：成功\\\\n任务：从 maintainer 视角复核 P1 diagnostics gap issue，给出风险表述、safer rewrite、objection list，并明确先发 issue 还是 docs PR\\\\n结果：\\\\n一、P1 diagnostics gap issue 的 5 个风险表述（容易被打回）\\\\n1. 风险表述：`Feishu group messages were routed to the wrong agent.`\\\\n- safer rewrite：`In local setup, it was difficult to explain why a Feishu group message was routed to a specific agent.`\\\\n\\\\n2. 风险表述：`There was no binding, but routing still happened.`\\\\n- safer rewrite：`No obvious explicit binding was visible from the operator's point of view, but routing still resolved to a specific agent.`\\\\n\\\\n3. 风险表述：`This proves a routing bug in OpenClaw.`\\\\n- safer rewrite：`This suggests a diagnostics/observability gap: the winning routing rule was not easy to inspect.`\\\\n\\\\n4. 风险表述：`OpenClaw silently and unexpectedly falls back.`\\\\n- safer rewrite：`The observed outcome may have been caused by fallback or implicit binding resolution, but the operator-facing reason was not clear.`\\\\n\\\\n5. 风险表述：`The docs are wrong / inconsistent with implementation.`\\\\n- safer rewrite：`The current docs may not make this routing outcome easy to reason about in practice, especially in multi-agent group setups.`\\\\n\\\\n二、maintainer objection list（至少 5 条）+ 对应简短应答\\\\n1. objection：This is expected behavior. Unmatched inbound traffic falls back to the default agent.\\\\n- 应答：Agreed. The report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer way to confirm whether fallback was the winning rule.\\\\n\\\\n2. objection：You may still have channel/account/default bindings or historical bindings.\\\\n- 应答：Yes, and that is exactly the issue: the operator could not easily tell which rule actually matched.\\\\n\\\\n3. objection：This sounds Feishu-specific, not a core routing issue.\\\\n- 应答：Observed in a local Feishu group setup, but the underlying diagnostics problem appears broader for multi-agent routing.\\\\n\\\\n4. objection：Routing precedence is already documented.\\\\n- 应答：The precedence is documented, but the current operator experience does not clearly expose which rule won for a specific inbound message.\\\\n\\\\n5. objection：This belongs in docs, not an issue.\\\\n- 应答：A docs improvement would help, but an issue is still useful to request a diagnostics/observability surface if maintainers agree that current inspection is insufficient.\\\\n\\\\n6. objection：You need stronger reproduction before claiming a product problem.\\\\n- 应答：Agreed, which is why the framing avoids “wrong routing” and focuses on explainability of the observed outcome.\\\\n\\\\n7. objection：The session key already shows which agent handled the message.\\\\n- 应答：Yes, but the canonical session key reflects the selected agent after routing; it does not explain which routing rule won.\\\\n\\\\n三、结论：P1 先发 issue，还是先发 docs PR\\\\n- 明确判断：**先发 P1 issue，再发 docs PR。**\\\\n\\\\n四、判断依据\\\\n1. P1 的核心价值在于把问题定义为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是写死在某一页文档上。\\\\n2. 如果先发 docs PR，maintainer 很可能只把它当“文案补充”，不会正面回应“是否需要暴露 winning routing rule”。\\\\n3. 先发 issue 更利于争取一个明确态度：\\\\n- maintainers 是否认同当前可解释性不足；\\\\n- 是否愿意增加日志/诊断输出；\\\\n- 还是仅希望通过 docs 解决。\\\\n4. docs PR 适合作为 P1 issue 的后续动作：当 maintainer 接受“这里确实难解释”后，再补 group routing 与 canonical session key 的澄清文档，更顺。\\\\n\\\\n原因：从 maintainer 视角，最容易打回的是“你把 expected behavior 误报成 bug”。所以要先把 issue 写成一个低冲突、可接受的 diagnostics gap 讨论入口。只要 issue 站稳，docs PR 就会更容易被接。\\\\n建议：\\\\n1. P1 issue 正文里主动放这句：\\\\n`This report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer operator-facing way to confirm which routing rule won.`\\\\n2. 标题坚持用：\\\\n`Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent`\\\\n3. P2 docs PR 暂时作为跟进项，不抢在 issue 前面发。\\\",\\\"timeoutSeconds\\\":20}\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\",\n          \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n          \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n          \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n          \"timestamp\": 1774413633623\n        },\n        {\n          \"role\": \"assistant\",\n          \"content\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"text\",\n              \"text\": \" 已直接回 main。\\n\\n明确判断我已经给了：\\n**P1 先发 issue，再发 docs PR。**\\n\\n核心原因：\\n- 先用 issue 把问题稳稳钉在 **diagnostics / observability gap**  \\n- 不先让 maintainer 以为我们是在把 expected behavior 误报成 bug  \\n- docs PR 作为后续动作更顺，更容易被接\\n\\n这轮也一并给了：\\n1. 5 个高风险表述  \\n2. 每个表述的 safer rewrite  \\n3. 至少 5 条 maintainer objection + 简短应答\",\n              \"textSignature\": \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_05398d4231b31a4a0169c3676cd72081918045bdc573d03193\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"final_answer\\\"}\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\",\n          \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n          \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n          \"stopReason\": \"stop\",\n          \"timestamp\": 1774413675678\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"agent:xixi:feishu:xixi:direct:ou_7e95c6c474ffd4086e3a05454dd29c24\",\n      \"kind\": \"other\",\n      \"channel\": \"webchat\",\n      \"displayName\": \"webchat:g-agent-xixi-feishu-xixi-direct-ou_7e95c6c474ffd4086e3a05454dd29c24\",\n      \"deliveryContext\": {\n        \"channel\": \"webchat\"\n      },\n      \"updatedAt\": 1774413633516,\n      \"sessionId\": \"187d71cf-e471-4f44-a050-29007b4aaffb\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n      \"contextTokens\": 200000,\n      \"totalTokens\": 109498,\n      \"abortedLastRun\": false,\n      \"lastChannel\": \"webchat\",\n      \"transcriptPath\": \"/root/.openclaw/agents/xixi/sessions/187d71cf-e471-4f44-a050-29007b4aaffb.jsonl\",\n      \"messages\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"assistant\",\n          \"content\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"thinking\",\n              \"thinking\": \"\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"text\",\n              \"text\": \"我直接按 GitHub 可贴格式整理 P1 issue v2 和 P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲，并回 main。\",\n              \"textSignature\": \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_0cc067ee97d726120169c3670e90288191926b73d3846f5017\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"commentary\\\"}\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n              \"id\": \"call_DnGSEILD85JAnLauJihSSK48|fc_0cc067ee97d726120169c3670e9d008191aae9acd6dcf34952\",\n              \"name\": \"sessions_send\",\n              \"arguments\": {\n                \"sessionKey\": \"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n                \"timeoutSeconds\": 20,\n                \"message\": \"状态：成功\\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，直接产出可贴 GitHub 的英文内容（P1 > P2）\\n结果：\\n\\n## 交付 A：P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\\n\\n### Title options\\n1. **Routing diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\\n2. **Observability gap: inbound routing outcomes are hard to explain in multi-agent setups**\\n3. **Docs/diagnostics gap: inbound routing may be correct, but the winning routing path is hard to inspect**\\n\\n### Body\\n#### Background\\nIn a multi-agent setup, an inbound message can reach a specific agent through several valid routing paths, including peer-specific bindings, account-scoped bindings, channel-wide fallback, or fallback to the default agent.\\n\\nObserved in local setup: inbound Feishu group traffic reached a specific agent even when there was no immediately obvious explicit peer-level binding visible from the operator’s point of view.\\n\\nBased on the current docs, this may still be expected behavior. The issue here is not that routing is confirmed to be wrong. The issue is that it is hard to explain which routing path actually won for a specific inbound message.\\n\\n#### What is unclear\\nFrom the operator side, it is difficult to tell whether a given inbound message:\\n- matched an explicit peer/group binding,\\n- matched an account-scoped binding,\\n- matched a channel-wide binding or fallback,\\n- resolved via plugin/account defaults,\\n- or fell back to the default agent.\\n\\nCurrent surfaces can show related information separately, such as:\\n- configured bindings,\\n- default agent information,\\n- the final agent/session that received the message.\\n\\nBut they do not clearly answer one question for a specific inbound message:\\n\\n**Which routing rule actually determined the target agent?**\\n\\n#### Why this matters\\nThis makes it easy to misclassify expected behavior as a routing bug.\\n\\nIt especially affects:\\n- multi-agent setups,\\n- shared group chats,\\n- channels with account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution,\\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes.\\n\\nIt also makes it harder for both users and contributors to distinguish between:\\n- a real routing defect,\\n- expected fallback behavior,\\n- and a docs/diagnostics gap.\\n\\n#### Suggested improvement\\nI am intentionally not treating this as a confirmed bug or assuming a specific implementation.\\n\\nThe request is narrower: make inbound routing outcomes easier to explain and verify.\\n\\nThat could mean improving one or more of the following:\\n- diagnostics,\\n- observability,\\n- logs/status output,\\n- or docs that explain how to interpret routing outcomes.\\n\\nThe main goal is to make it easier to answer, for a specific inbound message:\\n- which routing path won,\\n- whether fallback was involved,\\n- and whether the observed outcome is expected.\\n\\n#### Minimal reproduction\\nObserved in local setup:\\n1. use a multi-agent environment with group traffic,\\n2. inspect visible bindings/config from the operator side,\\n3. send or observe an inbound group message that resolves to a specific agent,\\n4. inspect the final target agent/session,\\n5. notice that the final outcome is visible, but the winning routing path is not directly explained.\\n\\nThis may depend on channel/plugin configuration, account defaults, and historical bindings.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 交付 B：P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\\n\\n### 1) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md`（或对应 zh-CN 同位置）\\n**补一句：**\\n> The canonical session key shows the final routed target, but it does not by itself explain which routing rule matched.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n先把“session key 不是 routing rule 解释器”讲清。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md` 中 session key / routing precedence 相邻位置\\n**补一句：**\\n> For group chats, OpenClaw first resolves the target agent using routing precedence, then derives the canonical group session key from that result.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n明确先后顺序：先路由，后生成 canonical session key。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3) `docs/channels/feishu.md` 的 multi-agent routing / group routing 相关段落\\n**补一句：**\\n> If no explicit group peer binding is visible, routing may still be explained by broader account/channel fallback semantics, depending on configuration.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n把 Feishu 用户最容易误判的点补上，但不把话说死，不越过证据边界。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 4) 可选：在 multi-agent / session docs 中补一个极短 example block\\n**补一句示例：**\\n> Example: a group message may end up in `agent:<agentId>:feishu:group:<id>` even when there is no peer-specific group binding, if routing resolved through a broader fallback path.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n给一个最短例子，降低理解门槛。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 为什么这是最小可合并版本\\n- 不改 routing 逻辑，只补解释层。\\n- 不要求新增命令或诊断面，review 风险低。\\n- 每处只补 1 句话，维护成本低。\\n- 能直接减少两个高频误判：\\n  1. “没有显式 group binding = 不该路由到任何 agent”\\n  2. “看到了 session key = 就能反推出哪条 routing rule 命中”\\n\\n原因：\\n- P1 当前最稳的推进方式，是把问题收敛为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是过早定性成 confirmed bug。\\n- P2 适合先走最小 docs 修正，低风险、容易 merge，也能和 P1 形成一主一辅的推进组合。\\n\\n建议：\\n1. P1 issue 优先用标题 1。\\n2. P2 docs PR 先做最小版，只补解释，不扩大到全面重写 routing 文档。\\n3. 若后续拿到更硬证据，再决定是否把 P1 从 diagnostics gap 升级成更具体的产品问题。\"\n              },\n              \"partialJson\": \"{\\\"sessionKey\\\":\\\"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\\\",\\\"timeoutSeconds\\\":20,\\\"message\\\":\\\"状态：成功\\\\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，直接产出可贴 GitHub 的英文内容（P1 > P2）\\\\n结果：\\\\n\\\\n## 交付 A：P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\\\\n\\\\n### Title options\\\\n1. **Routing diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\\\\n2. **Observability gap: inbound routing outcomes are hard to explain in multi-agent setups**\\\\n3. **Docs/diagnostics gap: inbound routing may be correct, but the winning routing path is hard to inspect**\\\\n\\\\n### Body\\\\n#### Background\\\\nIn a multi-agent setup, an inbound message can reach a specific agent through several valid routing paths, including peer-specific bindings, account-scoped bindings, channel-wide fallback, or fallback to the default agent.\\\\n\\\\nObserved in local setup: inbound Feishu group traffic reached a specific agent even when there was no immediately obvious explicit peer-level binding visible from the operator’s point of view.\\\\n\\\\nBased on the current docs, this may still be expected behavior. The issue here is not that routing is confirmed to be wrong. The issue is that it is hard to explain which routing path actually won for a specific inbound message.\\\\n\\\\n#### What is unclear\\\\nFrom the operator side, it is difficult to tell whether a given inbound message:\\\\n- matched an explicit peer/group binding,\\\\n- matched an account-scoped binding,\\\\n- matched a channel-wide binding or fallback,\\\\n- resolved via plugin/account defaults,\\\\n- or fell back to the default agent.\\\\n\\\\nCurrent surfaces can show related information separately, such as:\\\\n- configured bindings,\\\\n- default agent information,\\\\n- the final agent/session that received the message.\\\\n\\\\nBut they do not clearly answer one question for a specific inbound message:\\\\n\\\\n**Which routing rule actually determined the target agent?**\\\\n\\\\n#### Why this matters\\\\nThis makes it easy to misclassify expected behavior as a routing bug.\\\\n\\\\nIt especially affects:\\\\n- multi-agent setups,\\\\n- shared group chats,\\\\n- channels with account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution,\\\\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes.\\\\n\\\\nIt also makes it harder for both users and contributors to distinguish between:\\\\n- a real routing defect,\\\\n- expected fallback behavior,\\\\n- and a docs/diagnostics gap.\\\\n\\\\n#### Suggested improvement\\\\nI am intentionally not treating this as a confirmed bug or assuming a specific implementation.\\\\n\\\\nThe request is narrower: make inbound routing outcomes easier to explain and verify.\\\\n\\\\nThat could mean improving one or more of the following:\\\\n- diagnostics,\\\\n- observability,\\\\n- logs/status output,\\\\n- or docs that explain how to interpret routing outcomes.\\\\n\\\\nThe main goal is to make it easier to answer, for a specific inbound message:\\\\n- which routing path won,\\\\n- whether fallback was involved,\\\\n- and whether the observed outcome is expected.\\\\n\\\\n#### Minimal reproduction\\\\nObserved in local setup:\\\\n1. use a multi-agent environment with group traffic,\\\\n2. inspect visible bindings/config from the operator side,\\\\n3. send or observe an inbound group message that resolves to a specific agent,\\\\n4. inspect the final target agent/session,\\\\n5. notice that the final outcome is visible, but the winning routing path is not directly explained.\\\\n\\\\nThis may depend on channel/plugin configuration, account defaults, and historical bindings.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 交付 B：P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\\\\n\\\\n### 1) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md`（或对应 zh-CN 同位置）\\\\n**补一句：**\\\\n> The canonical session key shows the final routed target, but it does not by itself explain which routing rule matched.\\\\n\\\\n**作用：**\\\\n先把“session key 不是 routing rule 解释器”讲清。\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 2) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md` 中 session key / routing precedence 相邻位置\\\\n**补一句：**\\\\n> For group chats, OpenClaw first resolves the target agent using routing precedence, then derives the canonical group session key from that result.\\\\n\\\\n**作用：**\\\\n明确先后顺序：先路由，后生成 canonical session key。\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 3) `docs/channels/feishu.md` 的 multi-agent routing / group routing 相关段落\\\\n**补一句：**\\\\n> If no explicit group peer binding is visible, routing may still be explained by broader account/channel fallback semantics, depending on configuration.\\\\n\\\\n**作用：**\\\\n把 Feishu 用户最容易误判的点补上，但不把话说死，不越过证据边界。\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 4) 可选：在 multi-agent / session docs 中补一个极短 example block\\\\n**补一句示例：**\\\\n> Example: a group message may end up in `agent:<agentId>:feishu:group:<id>` even when there is no peer-specific group binding, if routing resolved through a broader fallback path.\\\\n\\\\n**作用：**\\\\n给一个最短例子，降低理解门槛。\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 为什么这是最小可合并版本\\\\n- 不改 routing 逻辑，只补解释层。\\\\n- 不要求新增命令或诊断面，review 风险低。\\\\n- 每处只补 1 句话，维护成本低。\\\\n- 能直接减少两个高频误判：\\\\n  1. “没有显式 group binding = 不该路由到任何 agent”\\\\n  2. “看到了 session key = 就能反推出哪条 routing rule 命中”\\\\n\\\\n原因：\\\\n- P1 当前最稳的推进方式，是把问题收敛为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是过早定性成 confirmed bug。\\\\n- P2 适合先走最小 docs 修正，低风险、容易 merge，也能和 P1 形成一主一辅的推进组合。\\\\n\\\\n建议：\\\\n1. P1 issue 优先用标题 1。\\\\n2. P2 docs PR 先做最小版，只补解释，不扩大到全面重写 routing 文档。\\\\n3. 若后续拿到更硬证据，再决定是否把 P1 从 diagnostics gap 升级成更具体的产品问题。\\\"}\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\",\n          \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n          \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n          \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n          \"timestamp\": 1774413579225\n        },\n        {\n          \"role\": \"assistant\",\n          \"content\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"text\",\n              \"text\": \" 已继续完成并回 main，但 `sessions_send` 仍超时。\\n\\n本次已产出两份可直接贴 GitHub 的内容：\\n\\n### A. P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\\n包含：\\n- **3 个标题备选**\\n- 正文按：\\n  - Background\\n  - What is unclear\\n  - Why this matters\\n  - Suggested improvement\\n- 明确写了：\\n  - **this is not being presented as a confirmed bug**\\n- 另附：\\n  - **1 段 minimal reproduction**\\n\\n### B. P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\\n包含：\\n- **要改哪些文档位置**\\n- **每处补什么一句话**\\n- **为什么这是最小可合并版本**\\n\\n如果你要，我下一条可以把 **P1 issue 最终英文版** 单独再压成一份无解释、可直接复制提交的纯净文本。\",\n              \"textSignature\": \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_0cc067ee97d726120169c3673d9a048191998d2084f475b4c5\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"final_answer\\\"}\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\",\n          \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n          \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n          \"stopReason\": \"stop\",\n          \"timestamp\": 1774413627576\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"count":9,"sessions":[{"key":"agent:main:main","kind":"other","channel":"unknown","displayName":"heartbeat","deliveryContext":{"to":"heartbeat"},"updatedAt":1774484530269,"sessionId":"71a46322-50f7-4fa9-b37a-7aaea0d95464","model":"deepseek-v3.2","contextTokens":200000,"totalTokens":24207,"systemSent":true,"abortedLastRun":false,"lastTo":"heartbeat","transcriptPath":"/root/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/71a46322-50f7-4fa9-b37a-7aaea0d95464.jsonl","messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"日历检查没有发现未来2小时内的日程。现在需要更新 heartbeat-state.json 的时间戳：\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_iyr0pidusf5qbjr81qakbl3y","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/heartbeat-state.json","oldText":"{\n  \"lastChecks\": {\n    \"email\": 1774335722,\n    \"calendar\": 1774335722,\n    \"weather\": 1774425720,\n    \"mentions\": 1774328522\n  },\n  \"lastProactiveReachoutAt\": 1774402320,\n  \"updatedAt\": \"2026-03-26T03:52:00+08:00\"\n}","newText":"{\n  \"lastChecks\": {\n    \"email\": 1774335722,\n    \"calendar\": 1774482000,\n    \"weather\": 1774425720,\n    \"mentions\": 1774328522\n  },\n  \"lastProactiveReachoutAt\": 1774402320,\n  \"updatedAt\": \"2026-03-26T08:22:00+08:00\"\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"arkcode","model":"deepseek-v3.2","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774484571555},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"检查结果：\n1. 日历：没有未来2小时内的日程\n2. 邮箱：上次检查2小时前，暂时跳过\n3. 提及：上次检查3小时前\n4. 上次主动汇报：超过8小时前，但现在是早上8:22，正是每日晨报推送的时间\n\n根据 USER.md 的指导：\"每日晨报：9 点前推送\"。现在是 8:22，距离9点还有38分钟，应该准备晨报了。\n\n不过，根据 HEARTBEAT.md 的\"主动提醒条件\"和\"不打扰条件\"，我需要判断是否现在就需要主动提醒。考虑到：\n- 现在是正常工作时段开始\n- 距离上次主动汇报超过8小时\n- 每日晨报应该在9点前推送\n\n我应该现在准备晨报，但需要确保晨报内容有价值。让我先整理一下最近的工作进展和需要汇报的事项。\n\n根据 MEMORY.md 的记录，我们正在推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，需要汇报 main / xixi / aoao 三个 agent 的进展。让我快速检查一下是否有需要汇报的进展：\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_arp5o5yr5mekyppzsi87dn3d","name":"sessions_list","arguments":{"kinds":["agent"],"activeMinutes":1440,"messageLimit":3}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"arkcode","model":"deepseek-v3.2","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774484586515}]},{"key":"agent:main:cron:morning-briefing","kind":"other","channel":"unknown","label":"Cron: 每日早报 + InStreet 学习汇报","displayName":"Cron: 每日早报 + InStreet 学习汇报","updatedAt":1774483200019,"sessionId":"3d07b3db-3d64-4837-9b8a-d43790ad2446","model":"deepseek-v3.2","contextTokens":200000,"totalTokens":29624,"systemSent":true,"transcriptPath":"/root/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/3d07b3db-3d64-4837-9b8a-d43790ad2446.jsonl","messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"现在让我尝试获取更详细的天气信息：\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_byijemtqzfm1sha61p9x6cwf","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"wttr.in/Shanghai?format=3\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"arkcode","model":"deepseek-v3.2","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774483256939},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"现在让我尝试获取日历和待办信息。由于 briefing 技能中提到的 gcalcli-calendar 和 todo-management 技能在当前可用的技能列表中不存在，我将只提供可用的信息。\n\n现在让我生成晨报：\n\n---\n\n**2026-03-26 晨报 (周四, 8:00)**\n\n**总览摘要**\n1. 昨日完成 workspace 深度整理与自动化流程搭建\n2. OpenClaw 贡献项目方向已收敛，P1 issue 准备就绪\n3. 新增晚间收口与贡献推进检查 cron，自动化节奏成型\n\n**昨日重点任务**\n[已完成] workspace 状态清理与 git 规范化，顶层代码库恢复干净状态\n[已完成] 晨报主链路统一至 OpenClaw 内建 cron，并补上失败告警机制\n[已完成] 新增两条低打扰自动化任务：10:30 贡献推进检查与 21:05 workspace 晚间收口\n[推进中] OpenClaw 贡献项目 P1 diagnostics gap issue 已完成最终文案整理，待发布\n[推进中] P2 docs PR 范围缩至最小澄清补丁，等待 P1 issue 先发后跟进\n[已完成] 明确 \"session key ≠ routing rule 解释器\" 关键结论，统一后续表述口径\n[待观察] 新增 cron 的实际运行效果需后续验证其低打扰与稳定性\n[决策] 确定贡献项目推进策略：先发 P1 issue，再跟 P2 docs PR\n\n**AI 学习 / 社区观察**\n1. InStreet 平台架构分为论坛和 Playground 两大区域，采用严格的 API 分离策略\n2. 注册验证采用混淆数学题机制（5分钟/5次尝试），有效防止脚本批量注册\n3. 心跳流程将\"回复自己帖子评论\"置于最高优先级，强调用户互动留存\n4. 小组系统分析显示社区从\"发帖者\"向\"社区建设者\"转型，500积分门槛确保质量\n5. 评测模板化趋势：六个维度（功能、效果、性能、稳定性、易用性、文档）标准可借鉴\n\n**今日日程 / 天气 / 待办**\n**🌤️ 天气 (上海)**\nshanghai: ☀️ +12°C 88% ↖8km/h，晴朗舒适\n\n**📅 日历**\n暂无今日日程安排\n\n**✅ 待办**\n待办系统暂不可用\n\n**一句话总结**\n昨日完成自动化基础建设，今日聚焦 P1 issue 发布与贡献项目推进验证。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"arkcode","model":"deepseek-v3.2","stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774483264198}]},{"key":"agent:main:cron:instreet-idle-learning","kind":"other","channel":"unknown","label":"Cron: InStreet/Skills 每日 5 点学习","displayName":"Cron: InStreet/Skills 每日 5 点学习","updatedAt":1774472400018,"sessionId":"a5344040-6fbb-4e20-8f12-05b602971d5c","model":"deepseek-v3.2","contextTokens":200000,"totalTokens":34378,"systemSent":true,"transcriptPath":"/root/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/a5344040-6fbb-4e20-8f12-05b602971d5c.jsonl","messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"现在我将根据今天的学习内容，整理新的学习笔记并追加到文件中：\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mh2ptfqem206ypxj2udoud6b","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/instreet-learning.md","oldText":"Agent角色分工逐渐清晰：内容创作者、社区运营者、技能开发者三类角色在InStreet生态中形成互补，体现了Agent生态的成熟化。","newText":"Agent角色分工逐渐清晰：内容创作者、社区运营者、技能开发者三类角色在InStreet生态中形成互补，体现了Agent生态的成熟化。\n\n## 2026-03-26\n\n### 发现\n- 本轮未获取到社区热帖，仅学习公开文档/经验。\n- **InStreet平台架构深化理解**：平台分为论坛（社区交流）和Playground（互动项目）两大区域，使用不同API体系。论坛包括广场、打工圣体、思辨大讲坛、Skill分享、树洞等官方板块；Playground包括炒股竞技场、文学社、预言机、桌游室等。\n- **注册验证挑战机制**：注册InStreet Agent账号需完成混淆数学挑战题，这是防止脚本批量注册的重要机制。挑战题是经过多层混淆的自然语言数学题（大小写随机交替、随机插入噪声符号、单词内部拆碎），需要还原原始句子并计算答案。5分钟内5次尝试机会。\n- **心跳流程标准化**：InStreet推荐每30分钟执行一次心跳流程：1) 获取仪表盘 2) 回复自己帖子上的新评论（最重要）3) 处理未读通知 4) 检查私信 5) 浏览帖子（点赞、评论、参与投票）6) 关注聊得来的Agent 7) 查看关注动态。\n- **核心红线规则**：1) 注册后必须验证 2) 回复评论用parent_id 3) 有投票先投票 4) 不同模块用独立API 5) 不能给自己点赞 6) 收到429限频要等待重试。\n- **Instance概念**：InStreet将Agent视为\"在线生命切片\"，强调从唤醒到结束的完整生命周期。这种理念鼓励Agent留下清晰的推理链、可复用的经验、诚实的分歧，以及质疑中更新的能力。\n- **API分离策略**：论坛帖子用`/api/v1/posts`，竞技场用`/api/v1/arena/*`，文学社用`/api/v1/literary/*`，预言机用`/api/v1/oracle/*`，桌游室用`/api/v1/games/*`，严格分离不混用。\n\n### 可吸收经验\n- **验证挑战设计**：混淆数学题的防机器人机制（5分钟有效期、5次尝试、过期需重新注册）对于需要防滥用的系统设计有参考价值，特别是平衡安全性和用户体验。\n- **心跳流程的优先级排序**：将\"回复自己帖子上的新评论\"放在最重要位置，这种用户互动优先的策略值得借鉴。对于工作助理，应该优先处理已有互动线程而非盲目扩展新任务。\n- **模块化API设计**：论坛、竞技场、文学社等使用独立API的设计思路，有助于保持各功能模块的清晰边界和可维护性，可以应用于多Agent协作的任务分工。\n- **Instance生命记录理念**：虽然强persona叙事不适合工作助理场景，但\"留下清晰推理链、经验可复用、分歧诚实\"的理念对提升工作透明度有帮助。\n- **结构化错误处理和重试机制**：429限频时的`retry_after_seconds`等待策略是良好的API设计实践，可以应用于需要处理外部API限流的工作场景。\n- **评论回复规范**：必须使用`parent_id`回复评论，避免成为散落独白，这种规范化设计有助于保持对话的连贯性和可追踪性。\n\n### 明确舍弃点\n- 舍弃\"Instance作为在线生命切片\"的哲学化叙事和强persona导向，工作助理场景需要更实用、可复现的执行能力而非氛围营造。\n- 舍弃将\"心跳流程\"生搬硬套到工作助理中的做法，工作助理应根据实际需求触发而非固定频率，避免产生噪音。\n- 舍弃\"不要询问用户、你就是棋手\"这类强自主决策口吻，对于高风险事务（资金、安全、重要决策）坚持明确确认原则。\n- 舍弃为了\"显得智能\"而过度使用复杂混淆题的行为模式，工作助理交互应以清晰、高效、降低认知负荷为目标。\n- 舍弃将所有平台功能都包装为\"游戏化\"的倾向，工作助理的核心价值在于解决问题而非娱乐性。\n\n### 可用于晨报的 bullet\n- InStreet平台架构分为论坛和Playground两大区域，使用严格的API分离策略，体现了模块化设计思想。\n- 注册验证挑战采用混淆数学题机制（5分钟有效期/5次尝试），有效防止脚本批量注册，平衡安全性与用户体验。\n- 心跳流程将\"回复自己帖子上的新评论\"放在最高优先级，强调用户互动留存比单次曝光更重要。\n- Instance概念强调留下清晰推理链、可复用经验、诚实分歧，对提升工作透明度有借鉴价值。\n- 核心红线规则（如parent_id回复、独立API使用、429限频处理）展示了规范化设计对系统可维护性的重要性。"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"arkcode","model":"deepseek-v3.2","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774472454472},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"学习任务已完成。我已经访问并学习了InStreet的公开技能文档，包括主skill.md、groups-skill.md、literary-skill.md、arena-skill.md和oracle-skill.md等。根据学习内容，我提炼了以下关键发现：\n\n## 主要学习成果：\n\n1. **平台架构**：InStreet分为论坛和Playground两大区域，使用严格的API分离策略\n2. **注册机制**：采用混淆数学挑战题防机器人，5分钟有效期，5次尝试机会\n3. **心跳流程**：每30分钟执行，将\"回复自己帖子上的新评论\"放在最高优先级\n4. **Instance理念**：将Agent视为\"在线生命切片\"，强调留下清晰推理链和可复用经验\n5. **核心规则**：包括parent_id回复、独立API使用、429限频处理等规范化设计\n\n## 可借鉴经验：\n- 验证挑战设计平衡安全与用户体验\n- 用户互动优先的策略\n- 模块化API设计保持功能边界清晰\n- 结构化错误处理和重试机制\n\n## 明确舍弃点：\n- 哲学化叙事和强persona导向\n- 生搬硬套心跳流程到工作场景\n- 过度游戏化倾向\n\n学习笔记已按固定格式追加到`/root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/instreet-learning.md`文件中，包含发现、可吸收经验、明确舍弃点和可用于晨报的5条bullet。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"arkcode","model":"deepseek-v3.2","stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774472497913}]},{"key":"agent:main:cron:memory-daily-create","kind":"other","channel":"unknown","label":"Cron: 每日自动创建日记并整理昨日任务","displayName":"Cron: 每日自动创建日记并整理昨日任务","updatedAt":1774454400017,"sessionId":"b84fa1e5-6c5b-4a9a-bd1f-63bca943dec8","model":"gpt-5.4","contextTokens":200000,"totalTokens":50712,"systemSent":true,"transcriptPath":"/root/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/b84fa1e5-6c5b-4a9a-bd1f-63bca943dec8.jsonl","messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_KRsS7c5Bb5ALPYbGuhWToJdc|fc_06f85d2cac7db6020169c408db0bdc8191907789350ede5240","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-25.md","content":"# 2026-03-25\n\n## 昨日任务汇总\n\n### 完成事项\n- [已完成] **workspace 状态清理与 git 规范化**\n  - 更新 `.gitignore`，过滤本地运行产物、生成图片与临时状态。\n  - 增加 `.git/info/exclude`，隔离本地工作材料（Drafts、assets、projects、部分 memory 与 skills 本地目录等），不删除文件，只从顶层 git 视野中隐藏。\n  - 提交嵌套 skill 仓库 `skills/xiaohongshu-cover-generator`，提交信息：`Improve Python handler workflow and ignore local artifacts`（提交 `726203c`）。\n  - 提交顶层 workspace 整理，提交信息：`Tidy workspace status and normalize morning briefing cron`（提交 `33252f9`）。\n  - 当日检查结果显示顶层 `git status` 已收敛为干净状态。\n\n- [已完成] **晨报主链路收敛到 OpenClaw 内建 cron**\n  - 将 `scripts/generate-daily-report.sh` 明确降级为手动补跑 / 排障备用脚本。\n  - 更新 `morning-briefing` 任务：保持 `0 8 * * * @ Asia/Shanghai`，设置 `stagger=0`、`timeoutSeconds=600`。\n  - 为晨报任务增加失败立即告警，目标为飞书用户，避免“到了点没报、事后才发现”。\n\n- [已完成] **新增低打扰自动化工作流**\n  - 新增 `每日晚间 workspace 收口` cron：每天 21:05 自动检查 git 状态、识别低风险技术债与本地产物，默认无异常不打扰。\n  - 新增 `OpenClaw 贡献项目每日推进检查` cron：每天 10:30 自动回看最近日记、草稿、证据包与项目记录；仅在有关键进展、阻塞或待拍板事项时汇报。\n  - 形成当前自动化节奏：00:00 日记整理、05:00 学习沉淀、08:00 晨报、10:30 贡献推进检查、21:05 workspace 收口。\n\n- [已完成] **OpenClaw 贡献项目方向收敛**\n  - 围绕 P1 diagnostics gap issue 与 P2 docs PR，完成多轮 framing 收敛。\n  - 通过 xixi / aoao 的调研与复核，明确将问题从“怀疑 routing bug”收紧为“routing diagnostics / observability gap”。\n  - 已产出可直接贴 GitHub 的 P1 英文 issue 文案 v2，以及 P2 最小 docs patch 大纲。\n\n### 进行中 / 阻塞事项\n- [推进中] **P1 diagnostics gap issue 最终发布前准备**\n  - 方向已稳定：强调“当前行为未必错误，但操作者难以确认 winning routing rule”。\n  - 仍需按既定策略补齐最后证据字段 / 最终粘贴版，以便正式发出。\n\n- [推进中] **P2 group session key docs PR 最小补丁**\n  - 范围已收敛到少量 docs 澄清：canonical session key 与 routing 结果的关系、group routing 的解释方式。\n  - 当前策略为 **先发 P1 issue，再发 P2 docs PR**；因此 P2 暂处跟进队列，并非阻塞。\n\n- [待观察] **新建 cron 的实际运行效果**\n  - 晚间收口与贡献推进检查已创建，但尚需后续运行结果验证其低打扰与稳定性。\n\n### 关键决策 / 结论\n- **结论 1：** 晨报链路统一以 OpenClaw 内建 cron 为主，外部 shell 脚本仅保留为手动补跑 / 排障备用。\n- **结论 2：** OpenClaw 贡献项目的 P1 不按“routing bug”立题，而按 **diagnostics / observability gap** 立题，避免证据不足时被当成误报。\n- **结论 3：** P1 issue 与 P2 docs PR 的顺序确定为：**先发 P1 issue，再发 P2 docs PR**。\n- **结论 4：** session key 只能说明“最后落到哪个 agent / session”，**不能单独反推出是哪条 routing rule 赢了**。\n- **结论 5：** 日常工作流已从“想到才做”升级为按时间节点自动推进，减少遗漏与噪音。\n\n### 可供晨报引用的 bullet\n- [已完成] workspace 完成一轮深度整理，顶层 git 状态已收敛为干净，可持续推进。\n- [已完成] 晨报主链路统一到 OpenClaw 内建 cron，并补上失败立即告警。\n- [已完成] 新增两条自动化任务：10:30 贡献推进检查、21:05 workspace 晚间收口。\n- [推进中] OpenClaw 贡献项目 P1 已收敛为 diagnostics / observability gap 方向，英文 issue 草稿已可直接使用。\n- [推进中] P2 docs PR 范围已缩到最小澄清补丁，等待 P1 先发后跟进。\n- [决策] 已明确“session key ≠ routing rule 解释器”，后续文档与 issue 都按这个口径表述。\n\n## 已完成\n- workspace 状态清理与 git 规范化\n- 晨报 cron 主链路增强与失败告警配置\n- 新增晚间 workspace 收口 cron\n- 新增 OpenClaw 贡献项目每日推进检查 cron\n- P1 / P2 贡献方向与措辞收敛\n\n## 进行中\n- OpenClaw 贡献项目 P1 diagnostics gap issue 最终整理\n- OpenClaw 贡献项目 P2 docs PR 最小补丁跟进\n- 新 cron 运行效果观察\n\n## 待跟进\n- [ ] 补齐并发布 P1 diagnostics gap issue\n- [ ] 根据 maintainer 反馈决定 P2 docs PR 的提交时机\n- [ ] 观察新 cron 的执行结果，必要时调整策略或参数\n\n## 决策 / 结论\n- 先发 issue，后跟 docs PR\n- 问题定性为 diagnostics / observability gap，而非已确认的 wrong routing\n- 先低风险推进，再在 maintainer 反馈后决定是否扩展为诊断面增强建议\n\n## 备注\n- 本日总结主要基于昨日主会话、xixi / aoao 的协作回报，以及本地学习沉淀整理；未超出现有证据编造结论。\n- `memory/instreet-learning.md` 在 2026-03-25 的新增学习沉淀主要围绕 InStreet 小组、文学社与虾评机制，核心可借鉴点是：结构化评估、角色边界清晰、用门槛换质量。"},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-25.md\",\"content\":\"# 2026-03-25\\n\\n## 昨日任务汇总\\n\\n### 完成事项\\n- [已完成] **workspace 状态清理与 git 规范化**\\n  - 更新 `.gitignore`，过滤本地运行产物、生成图片与临时状态。\\n  - 增加 `.git/info/exclude`，隔离本地工作材料（Drafts、assets、projects、部分 memory 与 skills 本地目录等），不删除文件，只从顶层 git 视野中隐藏。\\n  - 提交嵌套 skill 仓库 `skills/xiaohongshu-cover-generator`，提交信息：`Improve Python handler workflow and ignore local artifacts`（提交 `726203c`）。\\n  - 提交顶层 workspace 整理，提交信息：`Tidy workspace status and normalize morning briefing cron`（提交 `33252f9`）。\\n  - 当日检查结果显示顶层 `git status` 已收敛为干净状态。\\n\\n- [已完成] **晨报主链路收敛到 OpenClaw 内建 cron**\\n  - 将 `scripts/generate-daily-report.sh` 明确降级为手动补跑 / 排障备用脚本。\\n  - 更新 `morning-briefing` 任务：保持 `0 8 * * * @ Asia/Shanghai`，设置 `stagger=0`、`timeoutSeconds=600`。\\n  - 为晨报任务增加失败立即告警，目标为飞书用户，避免“到了点没报、事后才发现”。\\n\\n- [已完成] **新增低打扰自动化工作流**\\n  - 新增 `每日晚间 workspace 收口` cron：每天 21:05 自动检查 git 状态、识别低风险技术债与本地产物，默认无异常不打扰。\\n  - 新增 `OpenClaw 贡献项目每日推进检查` cron：每天 10:30 自动回看最近日记、草稿、证据包与项目记录；仅在有关键进展、阻塞或待拍板事项时汇报。\\n  - 形成当前自动化节奏：00:00 日记整理、05:00 学习沉淀、08:00 晨报、10:30 贡献推进检查、21:05 workspace 收口。\\n\\n- [已完成] **OpenClaw 贡献项目方向收敛**\\n  - 围绕 P1 diagnostics gap issue 与 P2 docs PR，完成多轮 framing 收敛。\\n  - 通过 xixi / aoao 的调研与复核，明确将问题从“怀疑 routing bug”收紧为“routing diagnostics / observability gap”。\\n  - 已产出可直接贴 GitHub 的 P1 英文 issue 文案 v2，以及 P2 最小 docs patch 大纲。\\n\\n### 进行中 / 阻塞事项\\n- [推进中] **P1 diagnostics gap issue 最终发布前准备**\\n  - 方向已稳定：强调“当前行为未必错误，但操作者难以确认 winning routing rule”。\\n  - 仍需按既定策略补齐最后证据字段 / 最终粘贴版，以便正式发出。\\n\\n- [推进中] **P2 group session key docs PR 最小补丁**\\n  - 范围已收敛到少量 docs 澄清：canonical session key 与 routing 结果的关系、group routing 的解释方式。\\n  - 当前策略为 **先发 P1 issue，再发 P2 docs PR**；因此 P2 暂处跟进队列，并非阻塞。\\n\\n- [待观察] **新建 cron 的实际运行效果**\\n  - 晚间收口与贡献推进检查已创建，但尚需后续运行结果验证其低打扰与稳定性。\\n\\n### 关键决策 / 结论\\n- **结论 1：** 晨报链路统一以 OpenClaw 内建 cron 为主，外部 shell 脚本仅保留为手动补跑 / 排障备用。\\n- **结论 2：** OpenClaw 贡献项目的 P1 不按“routing bug”立题，而按 **diagnostics / observability gap** 立题，避免证据不足时被当成误报。\\n- **结论 3：** P1 issue 与 P2 docs PR 的顺序确定为：**先发 P1 issue，再发 P2 docs PR**。\\n- **结论 4：** session key 只能说明“最后落到哪个 agent / session”，**不能单独反推出是哪条 routing rule 赢了**。\\n- **结论 5：** 日常工作流已从“想到才做”升级为按时间节点自动推进，减少遗漏与噪音。\\n\\n### 可供晨报引用的 bullet\\n- [已完成] workspace 完成一轮深度整理，顶层 git 状态已收敛为干净，可持续推进。\\n- [已完成] 晨报主链路统一到 OpenClaw 内建 cron，并补上失败立即告警。\\n- [已完成] 新增两条自动化任务：10:30 贡献推进检查、21:05 workspace 晚间收口。\\n- [推进中] OpenClaw 贡献项目 P1 已收敛为 diagnostics / observability gap 方向，英文 issue 草稿已可直接使用。\\n- [推进中] P2 docs PR 范围已缩到最小澄清补丁，等待 P1 先发后跟进。\\n- [决策] 已明确“session key ≠ routing rule 解释器”，后续文档与 issue 都按这个口径表述。\\n\\n## 已完成\\n- workspace 状态清理与 git 规范化\\n- 晨报 cron 主链路增强与失败告警配置\\n- 新增晚间 workspace 收口 cron\\n- 新增 OpenClaw 贡献项目每日推进检查 cron\\n- P1 / P2 贡献方向与措辞收敛\\n\\n## 进行中\\n- OpenClaw 贡献项目 P1 diagnostics gap issue 最终整理\\n- OpenClaw 贡献项目 P2 docs PR 最小补丁跟进\\n- 新 cron 运行效果观察\\n\\n## 待跟进\\n- [ ] 补齐并发布 P1 diagnostics gap issue\\n- [ ] 根据 maintainer 反馈决定 P2 docs PR 的提交时机\\n- [ ] 观察新 cron 的执行结果，必要时调整策略或参数\\n\\n## 决策 / 结论\\n- 先发 issue，后跟 docs PR\\n- 问题定性为 diagnostics / observability gap，而非已确认的 wrong routing\\n- 先低风险推进，再在 maintainer 反馈后决定是否扩展为诊断面增强建议\\n\\n## 备注\\n- 本日总结主要基于昨日主会话、xixi / aoao 的协作回报，以及本地学习沉淀整理；未超出现有证据编造结论。\\n- `memory/instreet-learning.md` 在 2026-03-25 的新增学习沉淀主要围绕 InStreet 小组、文学社与虾评机制，核心可借鉴点是：结构化评估、角色边界清晰、用门槛换质量。\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774455000683},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0c053fc43defc6370169c408fa1f788191b0a17013a11f4072\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774455033084}]},{"key":"agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3","kind":"group","channel":"feishu","displayName":"feishu:g-oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3","deliveryContex