arer way to confirm whether fallback was the winning rule.\n\n2. objection：You may still have channel/account/default bindings or historical bindings.\n- 应答：Yes, and that is exactly the issue: the operator could not easily tell which rule actually matched.\n\n3. objection：This sounds Feishu-specific, not a core routing issue.\n- 应答：Observed in a local Feishu group setup, but the underlying diagnostics problem appears broader for multi-agent routing.\n\n4. objection：Routing precedence is already documented.\n- 应答：The precedence is documented, but the current operator experience does not clearly expose which rule won for a specific inbound message.\n\n5. objection：This belongs in docs, not an issue.\n- 应答：A docs improvement would help, but an issue is still useful to request a diagnostics/observability surface if maintainers agree that current inspection is insufficient.\n\n6. objection：You need stronger reproduction before claiming a product problem.\n- 应答：Agreed, which is why the framing avoids “wrong routing” and focuses on explainability of the observed outcome.\n\n7. objection：The session key already shows which agent handled the message.\n- 应答：Yes, but the canonical session key reflects the selected agent after routing; it does not explain which routing rule won.\n\n三、结论：P1 先发 issue，还是先发 docs PR\n- 明确判断：**先发 P1 issue，再发 docs PR。**\n\n四、判断依据\n1. P1 的核心价值在于把问题定义为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是写死在某一页文档上。\n2. 如果先发 docs PR，maintainer 很可能只把它当“文案补充”，不会正面回应“是否需要暴露 winning routing rule”。\n3. 先发 issue 更利于争取一个明确态度：\n- maintainers 是否认同当前可解释性不足；\n- 是否愿意增加日志/诊断输出；\n- 还是仅希望通过 docs 解决。\n4. docs PR 适合作为 P1 issue 的后续动作：当 maintainer 接受“这里确实难解释”后，再补 group routing 与 canonical session key 的澄清文档，更顺。\n\n原因：从 maintainer 视角，最容易打回的是“你把 expected behavior 误报成 bug”。所以要先把 issue 写成一个低冲突、可接受的 diagnostics gap 讨论入口。只要 issue 站稳，docs PR 就会更容易被接。\n建议：\n1. P1 issue 正文里主动放这句：\n`This report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer operator-facing way to confirm which routing rule won.`\n2. 标题坚持用：\n`Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent`\n3. P2 docs PR 暂时作为跟进项，不抢在 issue 前面发。","timeoutSeconds":20},"partialJson":"{\"sessionKey\":\"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\"message\":\"状态：成功\\n任务：从 maintainer 视角复核 P1 diagnostics gap issue，给出风险表述、safer rewrite、objection list，并明确先发 issue 还是 docs PR\\n结果：\\n一、P1 diagnostics gap issue 的 5 个风险表述（容易被打回）\\n1. 风险表述：`Feishu group messages were routed to the wrong agent.`\\n- safer rewrite：`In local setup, it was difficult to explain why a Feishu group message was routed to a specific agent.`\\n\\n2. 风险表述：`There was no binding, but routing still happened.`\\n- safer rewrite：`No obvious explicit binding was visible from the operator's point of view, but routing still resolved to a specific agent.`\\n\\n3. 风险表述：`This proves a routing bug in OpenClaw.`\\n- safer rewrite：`This suggests a diagnostics/observability gap: the winning routing rule was not easy to inspect.`\\n\\n4. 风险表述：`OpenClaw silently and unexpectedly falls back.`\\n- safer rewrite：`The observed outcome may have been caused by fallback or implicit binding resolution, but the operator-facing reason was not clear.`\\n\\n5. 风险表述：`The docs are wrong / inconsistent with implementation.`\\n- safer rewrite：`The current docs may not make this routing outcome easy to reason about in practice, especially in multi-agent group setups.`\\n\\n二、maintainer objection list（至少 5 条）+ 对应简短应答\\n1. objection：This is expected behavior. Unmatched inbound traffic falls back to the default agent.\\n- 应答：Agreed. The report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer way to confirm whether fallback was the winning rule.\\n\\n2. objection：You may still have channel/account/default bindings or historical bindings.\\n- 应答：Yes, and that is exactly the issue: the operator could not easily tell which rule actually matched.\\n\\n3. objection：This sounds Feishu-specific, not a core routing issue.\\n- 应答：Observed in a local Feishu group setup, but the underlying diagnostics problem appears broader for multi-agent routing.\\n\\n4. objection：Routing precedence is already documented.\\n- 应答：The precedence is documented, but the current operator experience does not clearly expose which rule won for a specific inbound message.\\n\\n5. objection：This belongs in docs, not an issue.\\n- 应答：A docs improvement would help, but an issue is still useful to request a diagnostics/observability surface if maintainers agree that current inspection is insufficient.\\n\\n6. objection：You need stronger reproduction before claiming a product problem.\\n- 应答：Agreed, which is why the framing avoids “wrong routing” and focuses on explainability of the observed outcome.\\n\\n7. objection：The session key already shows which agent handled the message.\\n- 应答：Yes, but the canonical session key reflects the selected agent after routing; it does not explain which routing rule won.\\n\\n三、结论：P1 先发 issue，还是先发 docs PR\\n- 明确判断：**先发 P1 issue，再发 docs PR。**\\n\\n四、判断依据\\n1. P1 的核心价值在于把问题定义为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是写死在某一页文档上。\\n2. 如果先发 docs PR，maintainer 很可能只把它当“文案补充”，不会正面回应“是否需要暴露 winning routing rule”。\\n3. 先发 issue 更利于争取一个明确态度：\\n- maintainers 是否认同当前可解释性不足；\\n- 是否愿意增加日志/诊断输出；\\n- 还是仅希望通过 docs 解决。\\n4. docs PR 适合作为 P1 issue 的后续动作：当 maintainer 接受“这里确实难解释”后，再补 group routing 与 canonical session key 的澄清文档，更顺。\\n\\n原因：从 maintainer 视角，最容易打回的是“你把 expected behavior 误报成 bug”。所以要先把 issue 写成一个低冲突、可接受的 diagnostics gap 讨论入口。只要 issue 站稳，docs PR 就会更容易被接。\\n建议：\\n1. P1 issue 正文里主动放这句：\\n`This report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer operator-facing way to confirm which routing rule won.`\\n2. 标题坚持用：\\n`Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent`\\n3. P2 docs PR 暂时作为跟进项，不抢在 issue 前面发。\",\"timeoutSeconds\":20}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774413633623},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":" 已直接回 main。\n\n明确判断我已经给了：\n**P1 先发 issue，再发 docs PR。**\n\n核心原因：\n- 先用 issue 把问题稳稳钉在 **diagnostics / observability gap**  \n- 不先让 maintainer 以为我们是在把 expected behavior 误报成 bug  \n- docs PR 作为后续动作更顺，更容易被接\n\n这轮也一并给了：\n1. 5 个高风险表述  \n2. 每个表述的 safer rewrite  \n3. 至少 5 条 maintainer objection + 简短应答","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05398d4231b31a4a0169c3676cd72081918045bdc573d03193\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774413675678}]},{"key":"agent:xixi:feishu:xixi:direct:ou_7e95c6c474ffd4086e3a05454dd29c24","kind":"other","channel":"webchat","displayName":"webchat:g-agent-xixi-feishu-xixi-direct-ou_7e95c6c474ffd4086e3a05454dd29c24","deliveryContext":{"channel":"webchat"},"updatedAt":1774413633516,"sessionId":"187d71cf-e471-4f44-a050-29007b4aaffb","model":"gpt-5.4","contextTokens":200000,"totalTokens":109498,"abortedLastRun":false,"lastChannel":"webchat","transcriptPath":"/root/.openclaw/agents/xixi/sessions/187d71cf-e471-4f44-a050-29007b4aaffb.jsonl","messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":""},{"type":"text","text":"我直接按 GitHub 可贴格式整理 P1 issue v2 和 P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲，并回 main。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0cc067ee97d726120169c3670e90288191926b73d3846f5017\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_DnGSEILD85JAnLauJihSSK48|fc_0cc067ee97d726120169c3670e9d008191aae9acd6dcf34952","name":"sessions_send","arguments":{"sessionKey":"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8","timeoutSeconds":20,"message":"状态：成功\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，直接产出可贴 GitHub 的英文内容（P1 > P2）\n结果：\n\n## 交付 A：P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\n\n### Title options\n1. **Routing diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\n2. **Observability gap: inbound routing outcomes are hard to explain in multi-agent setups**\n3. **Docs/diagnostics gap: inbound routing may be correct, but the winning routing path is hard to inspect**\n\n### Body\n#### Background\nIn a multi-agent setup, an inbound message can reach a specific agent through several valid routing paths, including peer-specific bindings, account-scoped bindings, channel-wide fallback, or fallback to the default agent.\n\nObserved in local setup: inbound Feishu group traffic reached a specific agent even when there was no immediately obvious explicit peer-level binding visible from the operator’s point of view.\n\nBased on the current docs, this may still be expected behavior. The issue here is not that routing is confirmed to be wrong. The issue is that it is hard to explain which routing path actually won for a specific inbound message.\n\n#### What is unclear\nFrom the operator side, it is difficult to tell whether a given inbound message:\n- matched an explicit peer/group binding,\n- matched an account-scoped binding,\n- matched a channel-wide binding or fallback,\n- resolved via plugin/account defaults,\n- or fell back to the default agent.\n\nCurrent surfaces can show related information separately, such as:\n- configured bindings,\n- default agent information,\n- the final agent/session that received the message.\n\nBut they do not clearly answer one question for a specific inbound message:\n\n**Which routing rule actually determined the target agent?**\n\n#### Why this matters\nThis makes it easy to misclassify expected behavior as a routing bug.\n\nIt especially affects:\n- multi-agent setups,\n- shared group chats,\n- channels with account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution,\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes.\n\nIt also makes it harder for both users and contributors to distinguish between:\n- a real routing defect,\n- expected fallback behavior,\n- and a docs/diagnostics gap.\n\n#### Suggested improvement\nI am intentionally not treating this as a confirmed bug or assuming a specific implementation.\n\nThe request is narrower: make inbound routing outcomes easier to explain and verify.\n\nThat could mean improving one or more of the following:\n- diagnostics,\n- observability,\n- logs/status output,\n- or docs that explain how to interpret routing outcomes.\n\nThe main goal is to make it easier to answer, for a specific inbound message:\n- which routing path won,\n- whether fallback was involved,\n- and whether the observed outcome is expected.\n\n#### Minimal reproduction\nObserved in local setup:\n1. use a multi-agent environment with group traffic,\n2. inspect visible bindings/config from the operator side,\n3. send or observe an inbound group message that resolves to a specific agent,\n4. inspect the final target agent/session,\n5. notice that the final outcome is visible, but the winning routing path is not directly explained.\n\nThis may depend on channel/plugin configuration, account defaults, and historical bindings.\n\n---\n\n## 交付 B：P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\n\n### 1) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md`（或对应 zh-CN 同位置）\n**补一句：**\n> The canonical session key shows the final routed target, but it does not by itself explain which routing rule matched.\n\n**作用：**\n先把“session key 不是 routing rule 解释器”讲清。\n\n---\n\n### 2) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md` 中 session key / routing precedence 相邻位置\n**补一句：**\n> For group chats, OpenClaw first resolves the target agent using routing precedence, then derives the canonical group session key from that result.\n\n**作用：**\n明确先后顺序：先路由，后生成 canonical session key。\n\n---\n\n### 3) `docs/channels/feishu.md` 的 multi-agent routing / group routing 相关段落\n**补一句：**\n> If no explicit group peer binding is visible, routing may still be explained by broader account/channel fallback semantics, depending on configuration.\n\n**作用：**\n把 Feishu 用户最容易误判的点补上，但不把话说死，不越过证据边界。\n\n---\n\n### 4) 可选：在 multi-agent / session docs 中补一个极短 example block\n**补一句示例：**\n> Example: a group message may end up in `agent:<agentId>:feishu:group:<id>` even when there is no peer-specific group binding, if routing resolved through a broader fallback path.\n\n**作用：**\n给一个最短例子，降低理解门槛。\n\n---\n\n### 为什么这是最小可合并版本\n- 不改 routing 逻辑，只补解释层。\n- 不要求新增命令或诊断面，review 风险低。\n- 每处只补 1 句话，维护成本低。\n- 能直接减少两个高频误判：\n  1. “没有显式 group binding = 不该路由到任何 agent”\n  2. “看到了 session key = 就能反推出哪条 routing rule 命中”\n\n原因：\n- P1 当前最稳的推进方式，是把问题收敛为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是过早定性成 confirmed bug。\n- P2 适合先走最小 docs 修正，低风险、容易 merge，也能和 P1 形成一主一辅的推进组合。\n\n建议：\n1. P1 issue 优先用标题 1。\n2. P2 docs PR 先做最小版，只补解释，不扩大到全面重写 routing 文档。\n3. 若后续拿到更硬证据，再决定是否把 P1 从 diagnostics gap 升级成更具体的产品问题。"},"partialJson":"{\"sessionKey\":\"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\"timeoutSeconds\":20,\"message\":\"状态：成功\\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，直接产出可贴 GitHub 的英文内容（P1 > P2）\\n结果：\\n\\n## 交付 A：P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\\n\\n### Title options\\n1. **Routing diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\\n2. **Observability gap: inbound routing outcomes are hard to explain in multi-agent setups**\\n3. **Docs/diagnostics gap: inbound routing may be correct, but the winning routing path is hard to inspect**\\n\\n### Body\\n#### Background\\nIn a multi-agent setup, an inbound message can reach a specific agent through several valid routing paths, including peer-specific bindings, account-scoped bindings, channel-wide fallback, or fallback to the default agent.\\n\\nObserved in local setup: inbound Feishu group traffic reached a specific agent even when there was no immediately obvious explicit peer-level binding visible from the operator’s point of view.\\n\\nBased on the current docs, this may still be expected behavior. The issue here is not that routing is confirmed to be wrong. The issue is that it is hard to explain which routing path actually won for a specific inbound message.\\n\\n#### What is unclear\\nFrom the operator side, it is difficult to tell whether a given inbound message:\\n- matched an explicit peer/group binding,\\n- matched an account-scoped binding,\\n- matched a channel-wide binding or fallback,\\n- resolved via plugin/account defaults,\\n- or fell back to the default agent.\\n\\nCurrent surfaces can show related information separately, such as:\\n- configured bindings,\\n- default agent information,\\n- the final agent/session that received the message.\\n\\nBut they do not clearly answer one question for a specific inbound message:\\n\\n**Which routing rule actually determined the target agent?**\\n\\n#### Why this matters\\nThis makes it easy to misclassify expected behavior as a routing bug.\\n\\nIt especially affects:\\n- multi-agent setups,\\n- shared group chats,\\n- channels with account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution,\\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes.\\n\\nIt also makes it harder for both users and contributors to distinguish between:\\n- a real routing defect,\\n- expected fallback behavior,\\n- and a docs/diagnostics gap.\\n\\n#### Suggested improvement\\nI am intentionally not treating this as a confirmed bug or assuming a specific implementation.\\n\\nThe request is narrower: make inbound routing outcomes easier to explain and verify.\\n\\nThat could mean improving one or more of the following:\\n- diagnostics,\\n- observability,\\n- logs/status output,\\n- or docs that explain how to interpret routing outcomes.\\n\\nThe main goal is to make it easier to answer, for a specific inbound message:\\n- which routing path won,\\n- whether fallback was involved,\\n- and whether the observed outcome is expected.\\n\\n#### Minimal reproduction\\nObserved in local setup:\\n1. use a multi-agent environment with group traffic,\\n2. inspect visible bindings/config from the operator side,\\n3. send or observe an inbound group message that resolves to a specific agent,\\n4. inspect the final target agent/session,\\n5. notice that the final outcome is visible, but the winning routing path is not directly explained.\\n\\nThis may depend on channel/plugin configuration, account defaults, and historical bindings.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 交付 B：P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\\n\\n### 1) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md`（或对应 zh-CN 同位置）\\n**补一句：**\\n> The canonical session key shows the final routed target, but it does not by itself explain which routing rule matched.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n先把“session key 不是 routing rule 解释器”讲清。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md` 中 session key / routing precedence 相邻位置\\n**补一句：**\\n> For group chats, OpenClaw first resolves the target agent using routing precedence, then derives the canonical group session key from that result.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n明确先后顺序：先路由，后生成 canonical session key。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3) `docs/channels/feishu.md` 的 multi-agent routing / group routing 相关段落\\n**补一句：**\\n> If no explicit group peer binding is visible, routing may still be explained by broader account/channel fallback semantics, depending on configuration.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n把 Feishu 用户最容易误判的点补上，但不把话说死，不越过证据边界。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 4) 可选：在 multi-agent / session docs 中补一个极短 example block\\n**补一句示例：**\\n> Example: a group message may end up in `agent:<agentId>:feishu:group:<id>` even when there is no peer-specific group binding, if routing resolved through a broader fallback path.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n给一个最短例子，降低理解门槛。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 为什么这是最小可合并版本\\n- 不改 routing 逻辑，只补解释层。\\n- 不要求新增命令或诊断面，review 风险低。\\n- 每处只补 1 句话，维护成本低。\\n- 能直接减少两个高频误判：\\n  1. “没有显式 group binding = 不该路由到任何 agent”\\n  2. “看到了 session key = 就能反推出哪条 routing rule 命中”\\n\\n原因：\\n- P1 当前最稳的推进方式，是把问题收敛为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是过早定性成 confirmed bug。\\n- P2 适合先走最小 docs 修正，低风险、容易 merge，也能和 P1 形成一主一辅的推进组合。\\n\\n建议：\\n1. P1 issue 优先用标题 1。\\n2. P2 docs PR 先做最小版，只补解释，不扩大到全面重写 routing 文档。\\n3. 若后续拿到更硬证据，再决定是否把 P1 从 diagnostics gap 升级成更具体的产品问题。\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774413579225},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":" 已继续完成并回 main，但 `sessions_send` 仍超时。\n\n本次已产出两份可直接贴 GitHub 的内容：\n\n### A. P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\n包含：\n- **3 个标题备选**\n- 正文按：\n  - Background\n  - What is unclear\n  - Why this matters\n  - Suggested improvement\n- 明确写了：\n  - **this is not being presented as a confirmed bug**\n- 另附：\n  - **1 段 minimal reproduction**\n\n### B. P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\n包含：\n- **要改哪些文档位置**\n- **每处补什么一句话**\n- **为什么这是最小可合并版本**\n\n如果你要，我下一条可以把 **P1 issue 最终英文版** 单独再压成一份无解释、可直接复制提交的纯净文本。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0cc067ee97d726120169c3673d9a048191998d2084f475b4c5\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774413627576}]}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774484608972}}
